# ForgeShield review artifact policy (CC-14)

ForgeShield recognizes exactly two review artifact tiers. These are
defined in code at
`src/forge_security/artifact_integrity/review_artifacts.py` and
enforced at the activation boundary by
`src/forge_security/lifecycle/activation_guard.py`. **Do not** invent
a third tier, and do not paper over a violation by widening
`POLICIES`.

## Tiers

- **`LEGACY_UNSIGNED`** -- pre-FS contract pipeline output. No
  detached signature, no signed manifest. Treat as best-effort
  provenance only.
- **`SIGNED_V1`** -- post-FS-12 output. Detached signature over a
  manifest that pins the artifact bytes by hash. Treat as the
  baseline going forward.

## Per-product rules (current)

| Product       | Accepts                       | Notes                                                                                  |
|---------------|-------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| contract-iq   | LEGACY_UNSIGNED, SIGNED_V1    | ContractForge pilot only. Tighten when FS-1 lands.                                     |
| nativeforge   | LEGACY_UNSIGNED, SIGNED_V1    | **NativeForge FS-12 must drop LEGACY_UNSIGNED** and tighten the activation guard.      |
| docketforge   | SIGNED_V1 only                | **No exceptions, ever.** SIGNED_V1 required at every artifact position from day one. |
| grantforge    | SIGNED_V1 only                | Default for new products until they earn a pilot exception.                            |

## Rules for agents and contributors

1. **Never** add `LEGACY_UNSIGNED` to DocketForge, GrantForge, or any
   future product. The defensive check in `is_tier_accepted` will
   reject it for DocketForge regardless, but the policy table must
   match.
2. When you see `LEGACY_UNSIGNED` referenced outside ContractForge or
   pre-FS-12 NativeForge code paths, treat it as a bug.
3. The activation guard (`activation_guard`) must remain the only
   place product code asks "may I activate?". Do not bypass it by
   re-implementing tier checks elsewhere.
4. Tests in `tests/security/test_review_artifacts_policy.py` pin the
   current policy. Changes to the policy table require updating
   those tests in the same change.
